  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "n-client",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "CLIENT ZONE. One link, no password, opened on a phone.\nReads left to right as a project actually runs: the questionnaire right after signing, then the normal week, the stage going ready, the code, the stamp and invoice, life after launch, day 30.\nGaps to look for: is anything here you would still end up explaining on WhatsApp?"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-nochat",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 3185,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 830,
      "text": "DELIBERATELY ABSENT: no chat, no comments, no file upload, no tasks. WhatsApp keeps those.\nThe referral ask is parked, so day 30 is only the number and the quote."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-admin",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 1100,
      "text": "TEAM ZONE. Both of you, same access, no self signup.\nThe two screens worth arguing about: 'Admin: a stage' has the WhatsApp sign-off fallback, because clients will type ok done instead of tapping.\n'Admin: invoices' is where the numbering rule lives, and it is the one thing that is painful to change later."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-money",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 2800,
      "y": 1900,
      "w": 1100,
      "text": "MONEY PATH, end to end: mark ready, client agrees or you record their WhatsApp reply, invoice is created with the next number, you mark it paid when the transfer lands.\nNothing invoices before a sign-off. That rule is the reason this exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-invoice",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 840,
      "y": 40,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Printed from the browser, no PDF library.\nBank details are placeholders until you fill Settings.\nNo GST line while the GSTIN is empty. Fill it in later and this page grows a tax block, without a rebuild."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-intake",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1560,
      "w": 830,
      "text": "THE QUESTIONNAIRE. Sent the moment they agree, done before the kickoff call.\nFive sections, saves as you type, and 'I do not know' is a real answer everywhere.\nSection 5 grants access by ticking, and the page refuses to accept a password, a key or an OTP anywhere in it.\nStage 1 cannot be marked ready while sections are unanswered, which is what makes it happen without chasing."
    }
  ],
